{
  "$comment": "VAPP-279 (docs/round-7-contract.md): the rules of a `variant: strip` Tabs, HAND-AUTHORED and replayed by packages/exponential-ui/src/tabs-strip.test.ts (the TS reference the web renderers use) and apps/desktop/crates/eui-core/tests/tabs_strip.rs (the core, so gpui and the natives through the FFI). partition = which tabs keep an item (`widths` = each item's width, `available` = the strip's room, `gap` = the list gap, `overflowW` = the `+N` button's width, `active` = the active index or null) → `visible` (indexes in order; the rest fold into `+N`): the IDE's work-tab vectors (packages/domain-contract partitionTabs, EXP-1334), tabs pack in order until the next would not fit, the `+N` width + gap is reserved only once something overflows, the active tab always shows, one tab always survives. dropSlot = where a dragged tab lands: `centers` = each VISIBLE item's centre x (screen px, strip order), `from` = the dragged slot, `delta` = px moved since the drag started (screen direction), `rtl` → `slot` = how many other centres the dragged centre passed in reading order. keySlot = Ctrl/Cmd+Shift+`key` on slot `from` of `count` → `slot` (one place in screen direction; null past an end or for another key). reorder = a slot move over the `visible` array indexes → the `reorder {from, to}` payload (array indexes; null = no event).",
